Explanation of the change:

- We introduce a private flag `pointerMoveQueued_` initialized to `false`.
- In `relayEvent_`, we now detect `PointerEventType.POINTERMOVE` and, if no frame is yet queued, schedule exactly one `dispatchEvent` in the next `requestAnimationFrame`.
- Other pointer events (`pointerdown`, `pointerup`, etc.) are still dispatched immediately.
- This throttles the number of `pointermove` events to at most one per animation frame, restoring interactivity performance similar to OL 6.3.1 when many features or heavy style‐computations are in play.
